# The four failing seeds pass, each now reading 31 and 31: the loop waited one cycle and the interface's counter
# reached the comparator's. 33 runs, no failure.
# ONE HONEST OBSERVATION: the fixed lockstep reports 169 retired in all eight control runs where the committed
# test reported 169 to 171. Removing the settle moves the sample earlier; no assertion in that test depends on the
# exact count (it asserts retired > 0, the pair equal, no mismatches, and the tohost code).
#
# ================ THE MUTATION: the loop must REPORT a real gap, never invent equality ================
# MUT-RETSKEW1, one line of dv/auto_dv/tb/gen_bridge_if.sv in a second root: the retired counter takes one extra
# step once, so from then on one retirement exists that the comparator never consumes. A loop that waited for
# equality would spin to its bound and then have to fail; that is the behaviour under test.
# $ command grep -n 'MUT-RETSKEW1' $S/l33/l40_mut_root/dv/auto_dv/tb/gen_bridge_if.sv
#   61:      if (rvfi_valid) evt_retired_count <= evt_retired_count + ((evt_retired_count == 32'd10) ? 32'd2 : 32'd1);   // MUT-RETSKEW1
# $ command grep -h 'sources sha256' $S/l33/l40_mut_root/outC/config_opts.txt   [root C, its own build]
#   sources sha256 (dv/auto_dv env, tb, isa, gen_tb): 7ef155c3ddcab7fd
# $ cat $S/l33/l40_mutrun.log
